  <h2>How does ChiroCandy help chiropractors get new patients?</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    We run Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok campaigns aimed at your ideal patients, optionally layer
    Google Ads for high-intent search, then qualify and schedule leads with AI-CA support. Automated
    email and text follow-up keeps prospects moving toward their first visit.
  </p>
  <p>
    The leak in most practices is not “more leads.” It is slow follow-up, a weak offer, and ads that
    are not tied to a booking path. ChiroCandy treats acquisition as one engine: demand, response,
    and the first visit. That is the
    <a href="/frameworks/known-found-trusted/">Known / Found / Trusted</a> sequence applied to new
    patients, not a stack of disconnected vendors.
  </p>

  <h2>What is included in the new patient program?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Ad creative and campaign management:</strong>
      <a href="/services/facebook-advertising/">Facebook and Instagram ads</a>, TikTok where it fits,
      and optional <a href="/services/google-advertising/">Google Ads</a> for people already searching
      for care.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lead qualifying and scheduling:</strong> AI-CA support to answer, qualify, and book
      instead of leaving inquiries in a voicemail pile.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Online booking and payment options:</strong> a path from ad click to a confirmed first
      visit, not a generic contact form.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Automated nurture:</strong> email and text sequences in the ChiroCandy app so unbooked
      leads keep moving.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Educational video for authority ads:</strong> content that makes the practice known
      before the patient needs to choose.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What happens in the first 30, 60, and 90 days?</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    The first 90 days are a launch, then an optimization cycle, then a scale decision. Timelines
    below describe the work, not a guaranteed patient count. Results depend on market, offer, and
    how fast the office answers.
  </p>
  <h3>Days 1–30: launch the engine</h3>
  <p>
    Intake, offer, tracking, creative, and follow-up go live together. Paid campaigns typically
    start producing inquiries after launch; the 10–14 business day build window used on
    <a href="/done-for-you-program/">Done-For-You</a> is the same idea here: do not turn ads on
    before someone can answer them.
  </p>
  <h3>Days 31–60: fix what leaks</h3>
  <p>
    We review cost-per-lead, show rate, and which ads actually produce booked visits. Targeting,
    creative, and the booking path get adjusted. This is also when front-desk speed and offer
    clarity show up in the numbers.
  </p>
  <h3>Days 61–90: scale what works</h3>
  <p>
    Budget follows the campaigns that book, not the ones that only collect names.
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a> or
    <a href="/services/reactivation-campaigns/">reactivation</a> get added when paid social alone
    cannot cover the market.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is this program for?</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    Practice owners who want predictable new patient flow without building an internal marketing
    department. ChiroCandy has refined this system across more than 2,000 chiropractic and
    healthcare offices since 2015.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose <a href="/done-for-you-program/">Done-For-You</a> if you want ChiroCandy to execute ads,
    SEO, follow-up, and reporting. Choose the <a href="/training-program/">Training Program</a> if
    someone on your team can own marketing weekly. Get New Patients is the acquisition system both
    of those sit on.
  </p>
